# Day 05 — Web Requests & Network Traffic

## What I Learned

I learned the basic process that happens when a browser loads a website:

1. Browser parses the URL
2. DNS resolves the domain to an IP address
3. TCP connection is established
4. TLS handshake establishes encrypted communication
5. Browser sends an HTTP request
6. Server processes and responds
7. Browser renders the webpage

I also learned how security tools can monitor or protect different stages of this process.

